Q: SVG masked progress bar A: <p>I don't think there is much of a &quot;SVG mastery&quot; needed here. The moment you have the shape of a single &quot;bar&quot;, just put it into <code>mask-image</code> and let CSS do the repeat. Optionally <code>round</code> it to whole spaced tiles:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>progress {
 mask-image: url("data:image/svg+xml,&lt;svg \
  xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' \
  stroke-linecap='round' stroke='black' \
  viewBox='-5 -5 10 20' \
  stroke-width='9'&gt;\
   &lt;path d='M 0,0 V 10' /&gt;\
 &lt;/svg&gt;");
 mask-repeat: round;
 --bg: color-mix(in srgb, canvastext 20%, canvas);
 background: var(--bg); /* For Gecko. */
 color: selecteditem; /* For pseudos through currentcolor. */
 width: 5em;
 height: 1em;
 font-size: 2.5rem;
}

progress::-webkit-progress-bar {
  background: var(--bg);
}
progress::-webkit-progress-value {
  background: currentcolor;
}
progress::-moz-progress-bar {
  background: currentcolor;
}

html {
 color-scheme: light dark;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;progress max="100" value="65"&gt;65&lt;/progress&gt;

&lt;p&gt;

&lt;input max="100" value="65" type="range"
 oninput="
  document.querySelector('output').value =
  document.querySelector('progress').textContent =
  document.querySelector('progress').value = value
"&gt;

&lt;output style="font-family: monospace; top: -0.5em; position: relative;"&gt;65&lt;/output&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>This minimal POC uses native <code>&lt;progress&gt;</code> to keep accessibility and convey semantics, what may seem pretty lazy yet I'd argue it is the exact right thing to do here. Controlling colours is admittedly pretty cumbersome, but still worth it, because the alternative -- building faux <code>progress</code> from DIVs -- would demand ARIA bonanza…</p>
<p>Pseudos taken from <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/42292476">https://stackoverflow.com/a/42292476</a></p>
